<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hiempsal I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 117 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hiempsal I was a Numidian prince, the younger son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/micipsa">Micipsa</a>, who inherited a share of the kingdom with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adherbal">Adherbal</a> and his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurtha">Jugurtha</a> in 118 BCE. Quarrels over the division began almost at once, and Jugurtha had him murdered soon afterwards. His death began the conflict that drew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurthine-war">Jugurthine War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hiempsal-i.jpg" alt="Hiempsal I" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Numidian_coin_uncertain_kings.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
